{"classification":"mathematical-missing-denominator-grouping","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0256","math_ordinal":249,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The later equality J epsilon'(J+epsilon)=epsilon proves that both factors belong in the denominator; the printed linear notation otherwise denotes multiplication after division by J.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt263.tex:368","source_normalized_sha256":"bc81219b0f77090b066b6ae3a67e888833e18deb23523ee73bc73ba62e55d711","source_text":"$\\epsilon'=\\epsilon/J(J+\\epsilon)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt263.tex:366","target_normalized_sha256":"869dcde0b4481953fd412678f8a3d421a439643c7b8688e06e38f4b47487edd4","target_text":"$\\epsilon'=\\epsilon/(J(J+\\epsilon))$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S263"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-parameter-domain","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0257","math_ordinal":456,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"rho and theta are the two scalar arguments of phi and are used as real polar coordinates; neither is an R^2 vector.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt263.tex:674","source_normalized_sha256":"410db4128b6cd4d916e82437cd19853d77f3d3cde3a0ab4f90f135fc615b7482","source_text":"$\\rho$, $\\theta\\in\\BbbR^2$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt263.tex:670","target_normalized_sha256":"60c4632e97d6a9a255c6c09b1578a510289968d36d883e13f1641763b87f5a5f","target_text":"$\\rho$, $\\theta\\in\\BbbR$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S263"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-ambient-dimension","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0258","math_ordinal":470,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The point has two coordinates and is passed to g defined on R^2; the one-dimensional domain is incompatible with both facts.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt263.tex:692","source_normalized_sha256":"d285e1258c0cb8af2a9a2a53b3e46740bc3527b5c5ff8c295ae22ca1d3bad666","source_text":"$x=(\\xi_1,\\xi_2)\\in\\Bbb R$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt263.tex:688","target_normalized_sha256":"885d1a62f57038787aca362a6baa81464e0a281beb2ded93238bb5270ed4292d","target_text":"$x=(\\xi_1,\\xi_2)\\in\\Bbb R^2$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S263"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-integral-value","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0259","math_ordinal":477,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"An antiderivative of exp(-t/2) is -2 exp(-t/2), so evaluation from 1 to infinity gives 2 exp(-1/2), not one-half exp(-1/2).","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt263.tex:707","source_normalized_sha256":"84cb5312c1066e37ab95a3d1425ea8cc96dacfb7e3dcf627e455cc11d9edac61","source_text":"$\\int_1^\\infty e^{-t/2}dt=\\Bover12e^{-1/2}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt263.tex:703","target_normalized_sha256":"1d6816211c5aa4a2357e4f1b2cd037d2143a4ecb8b275e1b605b8e550b5204d0","target_text":"$\\int_1^\\infty e^{-t/2}dt=2e^{-1/2}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S263"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-normalizing-factor","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0260","math_ordinal":593,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The preceding perturbation estimate and cited inverse criterion yield the bound only after left multiplication by T_n inverse; this also supplies the stated nonsingularity conclusion.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt263.tex:889","source_normalized_sha256":"cc835805716812ba96ac8eddfe81a9d6dad97b2cb32e3bea22541845df141d70","source_text":"$\\|(\\alpha T(x)+(1-\\alpha)T_n)-I_r\\|\\le\\Bover12$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt263.tex:886","target_normalized_sha256":"a06b3740e420c99010bf280da1055291cdabf5716d3746627af7204356955230","target_text":"$\\|T_n^{-1}(\\alpha T(x)+(1-\\alpha)T_n)-I_r\\|\\le\\Bover12$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S263"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-function-factor","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0261","math_ordinal":753,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The convolution was defined from f and g, and expanding its integral gives one factor of each; repeating f would erase g from the asserted identity.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt263.tex:1101","source_normalized_sha256":"2b553f34151809c5db93215bf7c097d69c18116c54655ca63b5d0a4677d57335","source_text":"$h(xy)f(x)f(y)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt263.tex:1097","target_normalized_sha256":"479629b8d1fbb6a7786a79798403048f8eeb222236438d4b4fd7eff1e9bc3839","target_text":"$h(xy)f(x)g(y)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S263"}
{"classification":"mathematical-unmatched-delimiter","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0262","math_ordinal":764,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH26-COMPLETE-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The closing parenthesis has no opening partner inside the integral and is a typographical delimiter error.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt263.tex:1114","source_normalized_sha256":"3418d836f3735dbe22aee6850abe085be9cf03fa11395ce3ccb71fbd8a3d51b4","source_text":"$\\mu_1E_{\\theta})d\\theta$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt263.tex:1110","target_normalized_sha256":"a0bc5a4066e0cdf6dbfa932fa71af9866d9942c7de457d56ea1f4d8e34c04263","target_text":"$\\mu_1E_{\\theta}d\\theta$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S263"}
